omx-panel (0.2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * version 0.2.6 (#25, #24)
  * docs/worked-example: every output is the transcript or a committed file;
    Zynthian claims cite the source at its commit; the commands name the
    commit they ran at (#24)
  * examples/worked-example/transcript: what each command of the document
    printed, from the run of repeat.sh at 3ebf9b7 (#24)
  * examples/worked-example: repeat.sh runs the document commands and keeps
    each output; survey-lsp-mono.sh lays out every mono lsp plugin (#24)
  * examples/worked-example/lilv-modgui.py: the header comment has no em dash
    (#24)
  * docs: the worked example shows the mkdir it runs, and names the checkout
    in prose, not by a command whose output moves (#24)
  * examples/worked-example: the files docs/worked-example.md writes, and its
    lilv check (#24)
  * check-spdx: the worked example's command outputs are exempt, kept as each
    command wrote them (#24)
  * docs: a worked example, ZamComp (LV2) and LSP Limiter Mono (CLAP) from
    the scan to a generated panel, and Zynthian (#24)
  * modgui: a readout is drawn as a display, never looked up as a control
    input (#25)
  * modgui-test.sh holds a readout as a display with its range, no default
    and no port role (#25)
  * docs: a readout is drawn as a display, never looked up as a control input
    (#25)

